1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:02,681
This is Kioku.

2
00:00:02,681 --> 00:00:04,959
In Japanese, the
word means memory.

3
00:00:08,309 --> 00:00:11,042
At work, meetings,
documents and decisions

4
00:00:11,042 --> 00:00:13,827
pile up, and what
matters ends up lost.

5
00:00:16,477 --> 00:00:18,929
Kioku gathers everything
into a personal

6
00:00:18,929 --> 00:00:20,963
wiki: one page per project,

7
00:00:20,963 --> 00:00:23,926
per person, per meeting
and per decision.

8
00:00:26,576 --> 00:00:28,545
Claude writes these
pages and keeps them

9
00:00:28,545 --> 00:00:31,011
up to date, from the
sources you hand it.

10
00:00:33,661 --> 00:00:35,497
Then you simply ask a question.

11
00:00:35,497 --> 00:00:36,790
The answer comes from the

12
00:00:36,790 --> 00:00:38,334
wiki, with its sources.

13
00:00:40,984 --> 00:00:43,239
Every piece of
information follows the

14
00:00:43,239 --> 00:00:45,443
same path, through three layers:

15
00:00:45,443 --> 00:00:47,347
bronze, silver and gold.

16
00:00:47,347 --> 00:00:49,651
This is the medallion
architecture.

17
00:00:52,301 --> 00:00:53,799
To reach the gold layer,

18
00:00:53,799 --> 00:00:55,457
a page must pass a gate.

19
00:00:58,107 --> 00:01:00,191
An independent reviewer
checks where it

20
00:01:00,191 --> 00:01:01,732
comes from, its format,

21
00:01:01,732 --> 00:01:04,111
and respect for the
people it mentions.

22
00:01:06,761 --> 00:01:08,849
Whatever it holds
back is set aside,

23
00:01:08,849 --> 00:01:10,787
and waits for a human decision.

24
00:01:13,937 --> 00:01:16,370
Each domain, work or
personal life for

25
00:01:16,370 --> 00:01:18,555
example, lives in its own silo,

26
00:01:18,555 --> 00:01:21,238
with its own reviewer
and its own rules.

27
00:01:24,388 --> 00:01:27,023
A local dashboard shows
the whole wiki as

28
00:01:27,023 --> 00:01:29,605
a 3D graph: every
page is a point,

29
00:01:29,605 --> 00:01:31,752
linked to the pages it cites.

30
00:01:34,403 --> 00:01:35,108
Kioku.

31
00:01:35,108 --> 00:01:37,324
A working memory
that no longer gets

32
00:01:37,324 --> 00:01:39,187
lost: reviewed, sourced,

33
00:01:39,187 --> 00:01:41,199
and always one question away.
